{"title":"Meridian Hospitals","sub":"How can a hospital chain double its revenue in five years?","type":"Growth strategy","industry":"Healthcare","geo":"India","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"35 min","skills":"Revenue trees · sizing growth levers · capital constraints","prompt":"Meridian runs 12 private multi-specialty hospitals in South India with revenue of $300M a year. The board wants to double revenue to $600M within five years without hurting quality. How should Meridian get there?","clarify":[{"q":"Revenue breakdown?","a":"Inpatient 65%, outpatient consultations 20%, pharmacy 10%, diagnostics 5%."},{"q":"Capacity?","a":"2,400 beds. Average bed occupancy 62%; well-run peers in the region reach 75%."},{"q":"Profitability / funding?","a":"EBITDA margin 18% (~$54M). Moderate debt; the board is open to raising more."},{"q":"Where?","a":"Mostly large cities (Bengaluru, Chennai, Hyderabad). No presence yet in smaller (tier-2) cities."}],"structure":{"root":"+$300M revenue in 5 years: where from?","branches":[{"head":"Existing hospitals","items":["Fill empty beds (occupancy 62% → 75%)","Higher-value treatments (case mix)","Grow outpatient, pharmacy, diagnostics"]},{"head":"New capacity","items":["Build new hospitals","Expand existing sites"]},{"head":"Inorganic","items":["Buy smaller hospitals","Partnerships / management contracts"]},{"head":"New services","items":["Home care, telemedicine","Standalone diagnostic centres"]}]},"hypothesis":"Existing hospitals can deliver maybe a third of the growth through occupancy. The rest needs new beds, and given the 5-year time frame, buying hospitals may beat building them.","questions":[{"q":"Occupancy varies a lot by hospital. What do you see?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"390.723437pt\" height=\"174.004pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 390.723437 174.004\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-