148.896 L 367.29071 82.896 L 345.280233 82.896 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p3ad621280b)\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_15\"><path d=\"M 26.403437 148.896 L 26.403437 10.296 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_16\"><path d=\"M 26.403438 148.896 L 383.523438 148.896 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_18\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(48.573279 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_19\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(76.162001 21.697231) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_20\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(104.411348 26.774154) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_21\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(131.03257 28.466462) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_22\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(158.418167 30.158769) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_23\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(185.891264 31.851077) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_24\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(213.432486 35.235692) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_25\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(240.993083 38.620308) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_26\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(268.350555 45.389538) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_27\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(296.066777 72.466462) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(64.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_28\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(324.316124 77.543385) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(64.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_29\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(351.089846 80.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(64.09375 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p3ad621280b\"><rect x=\"26.403437\" y=\"10.296\" width=\"357.12\" height=\"138.6\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Bed occupancy by hospital, %","note":"H10-H12 opened in the last 3 years in newer parts of the cities."},"answer":"<p>Nine hospitals sit between 60% and 78%. Three newer ones (H10-H12) are around 40% and drag the average down to 62%. <b>So-what:</b> the occupancy problem is concentrated. Typical causes for new hospitals: not enough well-known doctors, and few referrals from local GPs. Fixing these three is the fastest growth lever available.</p>"},{"q":"How much revenue would Meridian gain by raising average occupancy from 62% to 75%?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Inpatient revenue = 65% × $300M = $195M. Assuming revenue grows in line with occupied beds: $195M × 75/62 ≈ $236M → <b>+$41M</b>.</p> <p>If the other streams (outpatient, pharmacy, diagnostics: $105M) grow ~10% a year organically: $105M × 1.1⁵ ≈ $169M → <b>+$64M</b>.</p> <p>Existing hospitals ≈ <b>+$105M</b>. Gap still to fill ≈ <b>$195M</b>. <b>So-what:</b> around two-thirds of the target needs new capacity.</p><p>Note: a 75% <i>average</i> means every hospital at the peer benchmark. Lifting only H10-H12 to 75% takes the average to about 70% (about +$26M); the nine established hospitals (about 69%) must also rise.</p>"},{"q":"Here are two ways to add capacity. How would you fill the remaining $195M?","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["Per hospital","Build new (big city)","Buy existing (tier-2 city)"],"rows":[["Cost","$40M","$37.5M (1.5× revenue)"],["Revenue at maturity","$35M","$25M today; ~$35M after upgrade"],["Time to full revenue","4 years","Immediate, upgrade over 2 years"],["Main risk","Construction delays","Quality, integration, culture"]],"title":"Exhibit 2 · Build vs buy","note":null,"align":["l","r","r"],"boldLast":false},"answer":"<p>A hospital built in year 1 only matures in year 5, so building alone is too slow: ~5-6 new hospitals ($200-240M) all opened in year 1.</p> <p><b>Buying</b> gives revenue straight away: about 4 acquisitions at ~$35M each after upgrade ≈ $140M for ~$150M. Add 2 new builds in big cities for ≈ $55-70M by year 5 → total ≈ <b>$195-210M</b>.</p> <p><b>Funding:</b> ~$230M over 5 years, plus upgrade capex for the acquired hospitals (ask the interviewer), against ~$54M+ a year of EBITDA. Doable with some debt, but tight. Look at asset-light options (management contracts) to reduce the capital needed.</p>"}],"reco":"Meridian can reach $600M, but it can't build its way there in five years. I recommend three steps: (1) lift occupancy across all 12 hospitals to the 75% peer benchmark, starting with the three under-filled ones (+~$40M; fixing only those three gives about +$26M), alongside organic growth in outpatient, pharmacy and diagnostics (+~$65M); (2) buy about four hospitals in tier-2 cities (+~$140M), which also opens new markets; (3) build two flagship hospitals in big cities (+~$60M by year 5). Total investment is about $230M. The biggest risk is keeping quality consistent across acquired hospitals, so next steps are a clinical-quality checklist for acquisitions and a shortlist of targets.","great":["Sizes each lever, adds them up, and names the remaining gap","Notices that new builds take 4 years to mature","Checks whether the plan can be funded","Mentions quality, the client's own constraint"],"id":3,"slug":"meridian-hospitals"}